            <span id="algorithm1.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.11.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,r,o)\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,r,o)\in R</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.12.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\notin V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\notin V</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            Add <math id="algorithm1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s-r-o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s-r-o)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algorithm1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\leftarrow V\cup\{o\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\leftarrow V\cup\{o\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B.\text{append}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext>append</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B.\text{append}(o)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Filtered entities from <math id="algorithm1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
            Clear <math id="algorithm1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.4.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.17.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>External Retrieval</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the LLM can attempt to answer the original question <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> using only the information encoded in the knowledge graph <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, its internal knowledge base may be insufficient to generate a fully accurate answer. To address this limitation and enhance the factuality of the LLM’s responses, we introduce an external retrieval mechanism that incorporates knowledge from Wikipedia and Google Search.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The LLM is allowed to iteratively improve the knowledge graph up to a limited number of times. In each iteration, the LLM selects a triplet from the graph and chooses one of two possible actions: <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correct</span> or <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expand</span>. <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correct</span> refers to improving the accuracy of a triplet that may contain errors, while <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expand</span> involves adding new related triplets based on the existing ones. Specifically, we construct a search query from the selected triplet <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,r,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,r,o)</annotation></semantics></math> in the form of ’s, r, o’, and retrieve the top <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> most relevant search results using the BM25 algorithm<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Robertson et al. (2009)</a></cite>. The search context is then provided to the LLM, which returns the corrected or expanded triplet(s), which are merged into the graph. By leveraging external information, the LLM refines and updates the knowledge graph, resulting in an improved graph <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Answering on the Graph</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once the knowledge graph <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> has been constructed and refined, the LLM is prompted to generate an answer to the question <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> based on the final graph. This structured representation ensures that the LLM’s response is grounded in verifiable facts, whether they are internally derived or externally validated. All the relevant prompts used during this process are provided in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Prompts ‣ Improving Factuality in LLMs via Inference-Time Knowledge Graph Construction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
